<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African money market shortage below 9 bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.African money market shortage below 9 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank said the South African money market shortage fell to 8.605 billion rand on Saturday from 9.923 billion rand on Friday.</p>
<p>Banks kept their three-month NCD rates unchanged at between 17.00 and 17.10 percent offered, while the 90-day BA rate was quoted in a 16.40 to 16.65 percent range.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
